The '''Sundari shipping docks''' were located just outside the [[Mandalorian]] [[capital]] [[city]] [[Sundari]].<ref name="Corruption" />

In [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Order">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' states that the events of "[[The Academy]]" follow the second mission to Florrum featured in "[[Lethal Trackdown]]." However, {{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-clone-wars-chronological-episodeorder|text=''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' Chronological Episode Order}} establishes that the events of "[[Corruption (episode)|Corruption]]," which features the [[skirmish at the Sundari docks]], occur between "Lethal Trackdown" and "The Academy." Therefore, the second mission to Florrum must be followed by the skirmish at the Sundari docks. The events of "The Academy" are themselves followed by the [[Alderaan Refugee Conference]] according to ''Timelines''.</ref> a [[Skirmish at the Sundari docks|skirmish]] took place at the docks when [[New Mandalorians|New Mandalorian]] forces battled with a [[Moogan]] [[Mooga smuggling ring|smuggling ring]] who were bribing corrupt officials at the docks to allow [[slabin]] into the city.<ref name="Corruption">{{TCW|Corruption (episode)}}</ref>

In [[20 BBY]],<ref name="AFiN date">{{TCWcanondates|414}}</ref> a failed [[Confederate–Republic peace conference|peace conference]] was held in Sundari. During the conference, [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] and former [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] [[Lux Bonteri]] were chased across the [[city]] by [[Commando Droid Diplomat]]s. At the docks, [[Senate Guard]] [[Captain]] [[Taggart (Senate Guard)|Taggart]] and their detachment of Senate Guards repelled the [[BX-series droid commando|commando droids]], enabling the two adolescents to escape on the [[Phoenix (GX1 short hauler)|''Phoenix'']], the Republic delegation's<ref name="FiN">{{TCW|A Friend in Need}}</ref> [[GX1 short hauler]].<ref name="DB GX1">{{Databank|gx1-short-hauler|GX1 Short Hauler}}</ref>

In [[19 BBY]]<ref name="Old Friends Date">{{TCWcanondates|709}}</ref> during the [[Siege of Mandalore]], [[Ursa Wren]]'s [[Mandalore resistance]] forces took over the docks from the [[Shadow Collective]]. Tano ordered [[Commander]] [[Rex]] to assist Wren, to prevent [[Maul]] from escaping the city.<ref name="OFNF">{{TCW|Old Friends Not Forgotten}}</ref>

